    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115-a4">

                <pb facs="0197" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg123"/>

                <head>[Enclosure D.—Translation.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pontifical
                            Zouaves, Command of the Battalion No.</hi> 463,<lb/><placeName><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Velletri,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 7, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">General</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Zouave Watson (John) has been arrested at Veroli, and will be conducted
                    to-morrow morning, under good escort, to Rome.</p>
                <p>While they were in search of him at Trisulti, his garrison, he was arrested by
                    Captain de Zambilly at Veroli, where he was on leave.</p>
                <p>I have the honor also to inform your excellency that his name is not <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Waston,</hi> but <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Watson</hi>.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, general, your excellency’s most humble subordinate,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lieutenant Colonel
                    ALLET</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
